Welcome to MyOS (live disk).

The programs are Alpine Linux's (musl), running unchanged on the
MyOS kernel. You are "myos", in group wheel: use doas for root.
Work in progress: much is still missing. Shut down with: doas poweroff

ssh is installed (client and server). The live account has no password:
`passwd` before you expect a remote login. Root is not allowed over ssh.
The kernel does not yet listen on TCP, so sshd cannot accept a connection
until that lands (docs/gaps.md). The client can still reach another host.

A static web server (darkhttpd, /var/www/html, port 80) is installed and
off. Start it with: doas myos-httpd enable
(same listen/accept gap until the kernel has it).

